      "description": "South Africa's real GDP contracted 0.2% quarter-on-quarter in Q2 2026 (seasonally adjusted, constant 2015 prices), after growth of 0.4% in Q1 — ending six consecutive quarters of expansion. Mining (-3.0%), trade (-1.9%) and manufacturing (-1.8%) were the main drags; finance (+0.3%) and personal services (+0.6%) grew. On the expenditure side, household consumption rose 0.4%, fixed investment fell 0.2% and net exports subtracted 1.1 percentage points. The estimate is preliminary: Stats SA's rebased (base year 2022) and benchmarked national accounts, expected in October 2026, may revise it.",
